  "title": "Finishing the written answer",
  "body": " Finishing the written answer  Subtract from . Every column writes zero, so the answer row first reads . We would ordinarily write just . The worker needs directions for this last part too.  Rest one finger under the final zero, in the units square, and leave it there. With a second finger, start at the leftmost answer digit. If this is the units square, leave it alone: even an answer of zero must keep one digit. Otherwise, if its digit is zero, erase that zero and move one square right. Repeat. On reaching a nonzero digit, stop erasing. All the digits from there to the units square belong to the answer. The underline travels with the second finger; the arrow stays under the units digit. In the last picture the two fingers have met. That comparison tells us to leave the last zero.  For , the first zero disappears and the nine stops the erasing. For , the first digit is already nonzero, so nothing is erased. The two zeros inside that answer stay where they are. This is a short walk along the finished answer, after the right-to-left walk that did the subtraction.  "
