  "title": "The final construction",
  "body": " The final construction  Joel David Hamkins, Every function can be computable! , presents an alternative proof based on a suggestion of Vadim Kosoy: a program searches for a certificate excluding a finite pattern of its own behavior and is prepared to realize that pattern. This is the certificate reversal adapted in the final chapter. Hamkins’s The universal algorithm: a new simple proof of Woodin’s theorem explains the stronger universal enumeration phenomenon. See also The Modal Logic of Arithmetic Potentialism and the Universal Algorithm , arXiv:1801.04599 .  Chapter 8 adapts certificate reversal to one common quotient record, using the stated verification hypotheses and compactness. Its model realizes every standard prefix of a prescribed decimal; it need not extend a preselected model. Chapter 7 explains why ordinary forcing preserves existing computations, unlike the variation of nonstandard records used in the finale.  "
